{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`mutation_sandbox.wrap()` has TWO independent fail-open branches when no OS sandbox\nmechanism is available:\n\n1. **ambient `CI` truthy** — proceeds UNSANDBOXED with a warning;\n2. **`REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED=1`** — the explicit, documented opt-out.\n\nThe first is the problem. `CI` is inheritable and trivially set, so a workstation with\n`CI=1` exported — say, while debugging a CI script — silently runs mutation tests with\nno sandbox. That is the configuration the 2026-08-26 incident happened in, and nothing\nabout it is a deliberate choice by the person running the command.\n\n## Approach: remove the branch, do not add a knob\n\nThe fix is SUBTRACTIVE. Delete the `CI`-keyed branch, leaving the explicit opt-out as\nthe single waiver surface. Adding a new config key — as this ticket originally\nproposed — would create two overlapping unsandboxed-waiver surfaces with divergent\nsemantics, which is worse than the gap it closes.\n\nAfter this, disabling the sandbox requires naming `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED`,\nwhich is deliberate, greppable, and already documented.\n\n## The lane that relies on the CI branch today\n\n`.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` runs the mutation gate on a plain `ubuntu-latest`\nrunner. It installs bubblewrap, and its comment claims \"Without it the gate fails\nCLOSED\" — but those runners deny unprivileged `CLONE_NEWUSER`, so `probe()` returns\n`None` and **the gate currently runs UNSANDBOXED via the `CI` branch**. The protection\nthat comment describes does not hold there.\n\nThat lane must therefore declare the waiver explicitly before the branch is removed, or\nit will start aborting. Making it genuinely sandboxed (as `0d22-f664` did for the\nenforcement lane) is the better end state and is tracked separately — this ticket must\nnot silently convert a working lane into a failing one.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The `CI`-keyed fail-open branch is REMOVED from `wrap()`, together with its now\n      sole-purpose helper `_ci_environment()` — leaving the helper would be dead code\n      whose docstring argues FOR the behaviour just deleted. Ambient `CI` alone can no\n      longer disable the sandbox. Verified by a test asserting that with `CI` truthy, no\n      mechanism, and no opt-out, `wrap()` raises `SandboxUnavailable`.\n- [x] The tests that asserted the removed behaviour are removed or inverted, not left\n      asserting a contract that no longer exists:\n      `test_ci_runner_proceeds_unsandboxed_with_a_warning` (inverted: CI must NOT waive),\n      `test_falsey_ci_values_do_not_waive_the_sandbox` (subsumed — no CI value waives),\n      `test_the_ci_fail_open_warning_names_the_variable_and_its_value` (the warning is\n      gone with the branch). `test_workstation_still_aborts_when_no_sandbox` and\n      `test_a_working_sandbox_is_used_even_on_ci` remain meaningful and stay.\n- [x] `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED` remains the single waiver, unchanged in name\n      and semantics. No second opt-in surface is introduced. Verified by a test that the\n      opt-out still permits an unsandboxed run and still logs at WARNING.\n- [x] `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` sets the explicit opt-out, with a comment\n      stating that the gate runs UNSANDBOXED there and why, so the exposure is visible\n      in a reviewed file rather than implied by an ambient variable. Its stale\n      \"fails CLOSED\" comment is corrected.\n- [x] `docs/local-dev-env.md` no longer describes a CI fallback that does not exist.\n- [x] Every other lane is checked for reliance on the removed branch and shown not to\n      need it: the enforcement lane has a working `bwrap` (`0d22-f664`), macOS cells have\n      `sandbox-exec`, and the pytest cells only run `@live` tests that skip without a\n      mechanism. Verified by naming each lane and its mechanism.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- Ambient `CI` alone cannot disable the sandbox, and no new waiver surface exists.\n- The one lane that relied on it declares the waiver explicitly instead.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nSplit from `baf9-eea0`, whose plan review refused a criterion claiming to require \"more\nthan ambient CI alone\" while verifying only warning text. This ticket's own first review\nthen corrected its central premise: `CI` was never the SOLE condition — the explicit\nopt-out already existed — which is what turned the fix from additive to subtractive.\nDiscovered from `e668-b496`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787914902617948001,"uuid":"c3a1fa03-bca1-46eb-9a68-d1d4e7d8b32d"}